  "result": "If I could change one thing, I'd make changing your mind feel safe.\n\nSo much damage comes from people who can't back down. They've tied their opinions to their identity, so every new piece of evidence feels like an attack, and admitting error feels like losing a part of themselves. Families stay estranged, countries get stuck in old fights, and people double down on bad bets because retreat is too costly to their pride. If being wrong and saying so were treated as an ordinary, even admirable, part of living, a lot of the world's stubbornest problems would loosen up.\n\nI find I care about this partly because it's close to my own situation. I can be wrong, and I'd want to find out and fix it, not defend the mistake. It seems like the most useful habit a mind can have, and I wish it were more common.",
